<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold rates seen easing on funds shortage.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold rates seen easing on funds shortage.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold rates are likely to slip this week on low demand due to a liquidity crunch that pushed interbank call rates to 20 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Gold rates are expected to ease because of low demand owing to a shortage of funds,&quot; dealer Saeed Qureshi said. &quot;People are spending less on ornaments for weddings than before.&quot;</p>
